      "id": "1sedp9r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the supreme monetary authority and central banking institution of India.",
        "Commercial Banks are split into Public Sector, Private Sector, Foreign, and Regional Rural Banks (RRBs).",
        "RBI controls credit using Quantitative tools (Repo Rate, Reverse Repo, CRR, SLR) and Qualitative tools.",
        "Types of bank accounts include Savings, Current, Fixed Deposit (FD), and Recurring Deposit (RD).",
        "Modern digital banking infrastructure relies on systems such as NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, and UPI."
      ],
      "id": "f4cnj71"
